<title>USA: TABLE - Ryland Group Inc Q2 net decreases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Ryland Group Inc Q2 net decreases.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBIA, Md. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30,</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p>    Total revenues			    399,620	 414,254</p>
<p> Net earnings				     3,870	   5,427</p>
<p>Net earnings per common share:</p>
<p>  Primary					    0.22	    0.31</p>
<p>  Fully diluted				    0.22	    0.31</p>
<p>Average common shares outstanding:</p>
<p>  Primary				    15,772,000    15,955,000</p>
<p>  Fully diluted			    15,772,000    16,868,000</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>						Six months ended June 30,</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p>    Total revenues			    729,140	 741,687</p>
<p> Net earnings				     5,606	   6,366</p>
<p>Net earnings per common share:</p>
<p>  Primary					    0.30	    0.34</p>
<p>  Fully diluted				    0.30	    0.34</p>
<p>Average common shares outstanding:</p>
<p>  Primary				    15,886,000    15,949,000</p>
<p>  Fully diluted			    15,886,000    15,949,000</p>
<p>		  (amounts in thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  For the diluted earnings per share for the second quarter and first six months of 1997, the company said the conversion of preferred shares is not assumed due to an antidilutive effect.</p>
<p>Net income for the second quarter of 1996 included net gains of $2.2 million, or $0.14 per share, from land sales.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1996 included net gains of $2.9 million, or $0.18 per share, from land sales.</p>
<p>As of July 25 the company had repurchased approximately 940,000 shares of its outstanding common stock in accordance with its repurchase program announced on April 30.</p>
</text>
